uary 17, 1963) is a Taiwanese and American electrical engineer and business executive who is the co-founder, president, and CEO of Nvidia, one of the world's most valuable companies.","cites":["wiki:rev:1384611104:0"]},{"t":"2026-11-09T00:00:24Z","text":"Jensen Huang was born on 17 February 1963 in Tainan.","cites":["wd:Q305177:P569","wd:Q305177:P19"]},{"t":"2026-11-09T00:00:32Z","text":"Educated at Oregon State University, Stanford University, Aloha High School and Oneida Baptist Institute.","cites":["wd:Q305177:P69:Q861888","wd:Q305177:P69:Q41506","wd:Q305177:P69:Q4734192","wd:Q305177:P69:Q7093656"]},{"t":"2026-11-09T00:00:39Z","text":"Worked in Los Altos.","cites":["wd:Q305177:P937:Q864124"]},{"t":"2026-11-09T00:00:45Z","text":"6 awards on record, among them Queen Elizabeth Prize for Engineering (2025) and National Medal of Science (2026).","cites":["wd:Q305177:P166:Q4273323","wd:Q305177:P166:Q737051"]},{"t":"2026-11-09T00:01:04Z","text":"The Guardian headlined it: “Nvidia opens investigation after report CEO Jensen Huang was target of foreign intelligence”","cites":["news:guardian:75eee0dcbc87"]},{"t":"2026-11-09T00:01:12Z","text":"Al Jazeera headlined it: “Trump defends Nvidia CEO amid Chinese spying allegations”","cites":["news:aljazeera:480dfda54b0f"]},{"t":"2026-11-09T00:01:20Z","text":"Sources: The Guardian and Al Jazeera, Wikipedia articles, Wikimedia pageviews and Wikidata. Every caption links to the evidence it rests on.","cites":["wiki:rev:1384611104:103","views:en:Jensen_Huang:30d","wd:Q305177:P569"]}],"time":"story","spotlight":{"country":"CN","lon":106.34,"lat":32.5,"label":"China"},"chapters":[{"t":"2026-11-09T00:00:00Z","title":"What happened"},{"t":"2026-11-09T00:00:24Z","title":"Born"},{"t":"2026-11-09T00:00:32Z","title":"A life across the globe"},{"t":"2026-11-09T00:00:45Z","title":"Recognition"},{"t":"2026-11-09T00:00:55Z","title":"Connected"},{"t":"2026-11-09T00:01:04Z","title":"In the news"},{"t":"2026-11-09T00:01:20Z","title":"Sources"}],"pa